        <mxCell id="v1" value="&lt;b&gt;SSD-A4: Approve or reject a membership request&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Document:&lt;/b&gt; behaviour design, iteration 2, DA-12 (Student 3), v1.0 draft&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;FRs realised:&lt;/b&gt; FR-A-08, FR-A-10, FR-A-11, NFR-S-03.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Rationale:&lt;/b&gt; The moderator decides with the coarse locality outcome and any flags as evidence, never raw location. A reason is required for every decision, and the system applies a decision only while the request is still undecided, so two moderators cannot both apply one (membership state machine M02 to M08)." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;fillColor=#F7F9FC;strokeColor=#9AA5B1;fontSize=10.5;fontColor=#1D1D1D;" vertex="1" parent="1">
